IMPORTANT — scope of this license: it covers ONLY the original source code and
configuration (Python scripts, Dockerfiles, Triton `config.pbtxt`, notebooks).
It does NOT cover the medical image data under `yte/` and `yte2/` (JPEG images,
YOLO labels and CSV annotations). Those files are derived from the public
"VinBigData Chest X-ray Abnormalities Detection" / VinDr-CXR dataset
(columns `image_id, class_name, class_id, rad_id, x_min, y_min, x_max, y_max`),
which is distributed by its owners under its own terms (e.g. a credentialed
health-data license and/or the Kaggle competition rules) that may forbid
redistribution. Obtain the data from the original source and check its terms
before reusing or redistributing anything under those folders. The trained model
files (`*.onnx`, `*.pt`) are derived from that data and from Ultralytics YOLO
(AGPL-3.0) and carry the same caveats. NVIDIA Triton Inference Server images are
subject to NVIDIA's own license.
